splat-train* crates
===================

The crates under crates/splat-train* are derived from Brush
(https://github.com/ArthurBrussee/brush) at commit
1388f74c6fe0236f68ee4915564bf00e9d2e3747, Copyright (c) Arthur Brussee and the
Brush contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE
in this directory).

Mapping (fork crate <- upstream crate; library names are kept so code is unchanged):
  splat-train              <- crates/brush-train
  splat-train-render       <- crates/brush-render
  splat-train-loss         <- crates/brush-loss
  splat-train-cube         <- crates/brush-cube
  splat-train-sort         <- crates/brush-sort
  splat-train-scan         <- crates/brush-scan
  splat-train-dataset      <- crates/brush-dataset
  splat-train-serde        <- crates/brush-serde
  splat-train-serde-macros <- crates/brush-serde-macros
  splat-train-vfs          <- crates/brush-vfs
  splat-train-async        <- crates/brush-async
  splat-train-colmap       <- crates/colmap-reader
  splat-train-rrfd         <- crates/rrfd
  splat-train-lpips        <- crates/lpips

Changes made by Nullframe are recorded in git history of this repository.
Notable fork-level changes:
  - package names renamed to splat-train-*; Cargo manifests carry a derivation header
  - LPIPS VGG weights (burn_mapped.bpk) are not vendored; loaded at runtime from SPLAT_LPIPS_BPK

The marked neural appearance implementation and derived per-scene configurations
are derived from nerficg-project/efficient-gaussian-appearance at 4efbe67
(https://github.com/nerficg-project/efficient-gaussian-appearance),
Copyright 2026 The Efficient Gaussian Appearance Authors, Apache-2.0.
These portions remain Apache-2.0 and are excluded from the Vauss Preview License.
